.TH __CTPOOL_DESTROY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
__ctpool_destroy \- destroy a thread pool (internal)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadpool.h>

void __ctpool_destroy(ctpool pool);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Frees all resources associated with the pool. If neither
ctpool_shutdown_drain nor ctpool_shutdown_immediate was called
beforehand, performs a drain shutdown inline (waits for all queued and
active tasks to complete) before freeing.

After this function returns the pool handle is invalid. Use the
ctpool_destroy macro rather than calling this function directly, as the
macro also sets the handle to NULL.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
pool   Thread pool handle (NULL is a no-op)
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Must not be called concurrently with any other pool operation.
Calling ctpool_destroy (the macro) is preferred over calling this
function directly.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ctpool_destroy (3),
.BR ctpool_shutdown_drain (3),
.BR ctpool_shutdown_immediate (3)
